---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const meta = {
	description: "About Convex in Prod.",
	title: "About",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<h1 class="title mb-12">About</h1>
	<div class="prose prose-sm prose-cactus max-w-none">
		<p>
			I'm <a href="https://github.com/leventov">Roman Leventov</a>, a software and systems engineer with 15 years of experience. I've taken part in developing several databases and big data systems, such as <a href="https://druid.apache.org/">Apache Druid</a> and <a href="https://www.stardog.com/">Stardog</a>.
		</p>

		<p>
			In the last few years, I've been an AI engineer, i.e., developing systems with LLMs under the hood. Over the last year, I've adopted Convex and TypeScript as my application platform of choice.
		</p>

		<p>
			I've decided to start this blog to share what I've learned over the last year about using Convex effectively. See <a href="/posts/about-blog-and-my-app/">About the "Convex in Prod" blog and my application</a> for more details.
		</p>

		<p>
			I do consulting on AI engineering, Convex, and application architecture. Contact me at leventov.ru@gmail.com.
		</p>

		<p>
			I have another blog called <a href="https://engineering-ideas.substack.com">Engineering Ideas</a>, with philosophical and system design ideas. I'm also sometimes active on <a href="https://x.com/leventov">X/Twitter</a>.
		</p>
	</div>
</PageLayout>
